Texas 42 (mk5) — Copyright Jason Yandell

This repository is under two licenses. Every file says which, in its own
SPDX header or in REUSE.toml, and `reuse lint` checks that none is missing.

CC0 1.0 (public domain) — the science. Everything by default: the engine
(src/), Walt, the scenario player (scenario/: the planner, the referee, the
compiled core, the Lean proofs), Silas (silas/), the arena, the tournament,
the wiki, the docs, the scripts, the oracle era (forge/, gus/, champion/,
w42/ and the rest), and the data. Use it for anything; no credit required.
Full text: LICENSES/CC0-1.0.txt.

MIT — Zeb, the player built on Walt: the package in zeb/, and Zeb's layer
in scenario/ (the field net, its training, its posterior draw and reading,
and the make-then-margin tie rule). Full text: LICENSES/MIT.txt and
zeb/LICENSE. The field net's weights (zeb/net/) are CC0: they were
published CC0 on Hugging Face first, with the pour they were trained on.

A few files carry both (SPDX "CC0-1.0 AND MIT"): scenario/planner.py,
scenario/compiled.py, scenario/core/src/planner.rs,
scenario/core/src/python.rs and arena/walt_play.py are Walt with Zeb's layer
woven through them. Until they are split (issue #158), treat them as MIT.

Not ours: the agent skills that REUSE.toml marks LicenseRef-third-party
(LICENSES/LicenseRef-third-party.txt), and the quotations from Dennis
Roberson's Winning 42, which are his and appear here as citation.

The names. The code is free (CC0 / MIT). The names Walt, Zeb, and Plunge are
not licensed as the name of your product.

